        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1e598692-c178-543d-b2bb-eef119cc2d03",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Iron Rattler, Rattler, Son of Beast\n- Companies: Roller Coaster Corporation of America\n- Places: Six Flags Fiesta Texas, Kings Island\n- Concepts: hybrid wood and steel roller coasters, inversion, zero-g roll, barrel roll, looping wooden coaster\n\nFacts:\n- In 1992, Roller Coaster Corporation of America's first major project was the Rattler at Six Flags Fiesta Texas.\n- In 2000, Son of Beast at Kings Island opened as the world's tallest and first looping wooden coaster, and it became Roller Coaster Corporation of America's most famous coaster.\n- Iron Rattler is the first hybrid wood and steel roller coaster to feature an inversion that turns riders upside-down and then back upright.\n- Iron Rattler's inversion is a zero-g roll.\n- A zero-g roll is a combination of a loop and a roll.\n- A barrel roll is sometimes described as a combination of a loop and a roll.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "064b23a2-597e-5ac5-9fa6-5eeafd23af5f",
        "text": "Page: Iron Rattler. Sentence: It is the first hybrid wood and steel roller coaster to feature an inversion, in which riders are turned upside-down and then back upright.\nPage: Iron Rattler. Sentence: The inversion is a zero-g-roll, which is when the train goes through a combination of a loop and a roll.\nPage: Barrel roll. Sentence: It is sometimes described as a \"combination of a loop and a roll.\"\nPage: Roller Coaster Corporation of America. Sentence: The company's first major project was the Rattler at Six Flags Fiesta Texas in 1992, while their most famous coaster was the Son of Beast at Kings Island, the world's tallest and first looping wooden coaster when it opened in 2000.",
